<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augustus, Duke of Saxe-Weissenfels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1614–1680</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augustus was a son of Elector John George I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and administrator of the Archbishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a>. Under his father's will he received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weissenfels">Weissenfels</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/querfurt">Querfurt</a> and other lands in 1656, founding the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxe-weissenfels">Saxe-Weissenfels</a>. He built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neu-augustusburg">Neu-Augustusburg</a> palace at Weissenfels and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fruitbearing-society">Fruitbearing Society</a>, a German language academy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augustus-duke-of-saxe-weissenfels.jpg" alt="Augustus, Duke of Saxe-Weissenfels" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Benjamin Block · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:August,_Herzog_von_Sachsen-Wei%C3%9Fenfels_a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
